My attending physician shoves me one of his articles about strange research titled "Money causes brain activation, especially if others get less."
Or the feelings triggered by a monthly salary for employees depends on how much colleagues earn.
The research was carried out at the University of Bonna using magnetic resonances on the tomograph, and the results are published in the latest issue of the journal Science.
According to Bernd Weber, author of the study and leader of the Life&Brain neurocognics group in Germany: "The biggest activation occurred when the research participant reacted correctly and his colleague incorrectly."
The researchers observed that if they both succeeded, they received the same salary, the activation was moderate, but when one received double, the activation was higher.
I really don't know if this conclusion required so much science.
