Which insurance is right for me?
Car insurance, which protects the driver in the event of an accident, represents a significant expense, which depends on various factors, such as age, condition, gender, the length of possession of the driver's license, the type of vehicle to be insured or used, etc.
Having a car is just the beginning.
Choosing suitable car insurance is even more difficult than choosing a car model.
First of all, we need to clarify what we are talking about.
Car insurance is an agreement between an insurance company and an insurer.
This obligation takes the form of an insurance contract, which stipulates that the insurance company receives an agreed insurance amount in a certain amount for taking charge of paying damages in the event of an insured event.
The insurance premium is the price of the insurance, which is determined with regard to various factors, such as age, condition, gender, the length of possession of the driver's license, the type of vehicle that is insured or its use, etc.
Insurance companies set their prices based on statistics, so the greater the likelihood of an accident, the higher the insurance rate.
For this reason, both people over the age of 25 and women have to pay lower premiums, as statistics show that they have a lower risk index due to their caution.
In the same way, on the basis of controls, insurance companies concluded that persons living in marriage have fewer accidents than single drivers.
The way the vehicle is used will affect the frequency of journeys and thus the likelihood that it will have an accident.
The increase in the frequency of trips increases the probability.
There are many variables that insurance companies are considering when setting the price of premiums.
Therefore, the driver has to study the situation well in order to choose such insurance, which best corresponds to his insurer profile.
We will show here the most important variables for choosing this or that type of insurance, which, in addition to complying with the type of insured, will also be at a reasonable price.
People under the age of twenty-five encounter various disadvantages, such as little driving experience and a short possession of a driver's license, when they want to arrange premiums at an affordable price.
Although ideal for good coverage is insurance against all risks, there are also cheaper options.
The most careful drivers can choose insurance against all risks at a discount of premiums in order to obtain insurance coverage of all risks, but at a more affordable price.
This kind of contract would presuppose the client's participation in the payment of an insured event.
"Part of the payment of an insured event provided by the client will be determined in advance when determining the price of the premium, which will be all the higher the lower the participation would be," explains Luis Noguera, chief executive of First Europe in Spain, an internet insurance intermediary.
Another option is insurance extended to other traffic participants so that the client insures himself against damage caused to other persons, but not against damage to his own car.
In addition, he would be insured against theft, fire and loss of the vehicle.
Recommendations.
If you're under the age of twenty-five, try to be attentive and prevent crashes as much as possible, as this will affect your bonus and allow you to reduce premiums in the future.
The bonus is a reduction in the basic rate that the insurance company has.
In contrast, malus is an increase in the aforementioned basic rate.
"Bonus and malus will depend on the insurance company and its profits.
If the insurance company has had a good year, it will be able to afford to increase the bonus," Noguera explains.
After crossing the twenty-five-year limit, drivers find it easier when they go to get insurance, because the client's risk index decreases, thanks to the acquired experience.
For this reason, it is most recommended to arrange insurance against all risks at a discount.
“Young people usually can’t take advantage of pre-acquired experience when there is an accident, nor in proceedings,” assures the director of a European company in Spain, adding that most accidents occur in the second year of proceedings, when the "fear of a newcomer" has already been overcome.
However, if the client is married but does not yet have children, it is better to arrange insurance against all risks, if, of course, his economic situation allows.
Families with children are considered by insurance companies to be the clientele with the lowest risk index, and therefore their mark-ups will be lower.
In this case, the best insurance would be insurance against all risks with a premium discount (which could amount to 300 euros) or with a high bonus, insurance extended to other traffic participants, starting from the third year since the purchase of the vehicle.
"Their management is calmer and their purchasing capacity is higher, so they can afford the luxury of getting the highest discount," remarks Luis Noguera.
Retirements are advised insurance against all risks with a discount of premiums (which amounts to 150 euros) or insurance extended to other operating participants if a high bonus has been achieved.
It must be said that car insurance is important not only because it protects drivers in the event of an accident, but also because it represents a considerable expense, which is a compelling reason to properly study the insurance options that would suit us best due to our personal situation.
Celtic are trying to score at AC Milan, which marks an eight-final
